  * Also the CPU clocks (MSM8996 Pro, Linux drivers/clk/msm/clock-cpu-8996.c):
- * ABL leaves the perf cluster (CPU 2/3) on the 19.2 MHz XO. The register
- * state is logged; boot-arg sweetclk=1 then runs the perf PLL at
- * sweetclk_mhz (default 883: the rate Linux's early init sets before any
- * voltage regulator driver runs, i.e. safe at ABL's APC voltage).
+ * ABL leaves the perf cluster (CPU 2/3) on the 19.2 MHz XO, the pwr cluster
+ * at 1228.8 MHz and the CBF (cluster/memory fabric) on GPLL0 (~300 MHz), with
+ * the shared APC rail PM8994 S11 at 905 mV and both kryo regulators in BHS
+ * (clusters fed straight from S11). 905 mV is the CPR ceiling of the
+ * nominal band (DT qcom,cpr-voltage-ceiling), so its top corners are safe
+ * without touching the PMIC: perf 1363.2 MHz, CBF 1190.4 MHz. By default
+ * (boot-arg sweetclk=0 turns it off) the perf PLL starts at sweetclk_mhz
+ * (default 1363) and the CBF PLL at sweetcbf_mhz (default 1190, 0 = leave
+ * on GPLL0); both ran a full iOS session (boot 0095a). With S11 below 905 mV (or unreadable)
+ * the perf cluster gets 883 MHz (Linux's early-init rate, set before any
+ * regulator driver runs) and the CBF is left alone.
  */
